From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Petar Tijanic <Petar_Tijanic@comcast.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add wayland inputfd backend

Forward-port of the 0.2 "wayland input_fd monitor" support (SKY, Red Hat) to
libmanette 1.0. On a sandboxed Wayland client the process cannot open
/dev/input itself; the compositor owns the devices and hands over an evdev fd
via the wp_inputfd protocol while the client is focused, and may revoke it.

The fd lives in the evdev backend in 1.0, so the device-from-fd logic moves
there: manette_evdev_backend_new_for_fd() wraps an already-open fd,
manette_evdev_backend_change_fd() swaps in a fresh fd after a focus-out/in
cycle, and manette_evdev_backend_is_revoked() detects a revoked fd. The
wayland client (manette-wayland-inputfd.c + inputfd-v1.xml) is carried over
mostly unchanged; the monitor gains a wayland backend that creates/updates
devices keyed by the protocol uuid. It is added alongside the file/gudev
backend (which finds nothing on a sandboxed box) and gated by the new
wayland-inputfd meson option.
---
